@*
    Evidence viewer (DOCS-011).

    docs/design/README.md#contracts "Evidence image preview" requires explicit
    loading and source-preserving enlarged-image states, and that opening or
    closing a preview preserves Case context. It is an overlay, so the case
    page, its tab and its unsaved edits stay behind it; the enlarged view reads
    the same authorised URL as the thumbnail, so nothing is re-encoded.

    It reuses .reason-dialog-backdrop and the [data-reason-dialog] behaviour
    contract -- initial focus, focus containment, Escape, focus return -- rather
    than declaring a second overlay convention. Render it once per page; the
    triggers are the [data-evidence-item] links inside a [data-evidence-set].

    PDFs use an <iframe> because the deployed CSP sets object-src 'none'.
*@
<div id="evidence-viewer"
     class="reason-dialog-backdrop evidence-viewer"
     role="dialog"
     aria-modal="true"
     aria-labelledby="evidence-viewer-name"
     data-evidence-viewer
     hidden>
    <div class="evidence-viewer__panel">
        <div class="evidence-viewer__bar">
            <h2 id="evidence-viewer-name" class="evidence-viewer__name" data-evidence-name></h2>
            <span class="evidence-viewer__position" data-evidence-position></span>
            <a class="secondary-action" data-evidence-download download>Download</a>
            <button type="button" class="secondary-action" data-evidence-close>Close</button>
        </div>
        <div class="evidence-viewer__frame">
            <button type="button" class="evidence-viewer__step" data-evidence-previous>Previous</button>
            <div class="evidence-viewer__stage" data-evidence-stage>
                <img class="evidence-viewer__image" data-evidence-image alt="" hidden />
                <iframe class="evidence-viewer__document" data-evidence-document title="" hidden></iframe>
            </div>
            <button type="button" class="evidence-viewer__step" data-evidence-next>Next</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
